WEBVTT

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.340
<v Carl Robison>I think the biggest thing
is just recognizing that

00:00:02.420 --> 00:00:05.060
<v Carl Robison>we're going to have AI forever.

00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:08.500
<v Carl Robison>Like there's no getting
away from any of that.

00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:11.113
<v Carl Robison>If you don't know how to
use it, you're going to fall

00:00:11.193 --> 00:00:11.553
<v Carl Robison>behind.

00:00:11.633 --> 00:00:15.193
<v Carl Robison>That being said, if that's
all you use, you're useless

00:00:15.273 --> 00:00:17.076
<v Carl Robison>because anyone can use AI.

00:00:17.156 --> 00:00:23.406
<v Sterling Baird>so if I had an e-bike I
know myself well enough that

00:00:23.486 --> 00:00:26.846
<v Sterling Baird>I would probably start relying
on the e-bike intensively

00:00:26.926 --> 00:00:29.826
<v Sterling Baird>rather than getting a
workout that I need every day

00:00:29.906 --> 00:00:32.306
<v Sterling Baird>So it's so much easier to
be complacent when the tool

00:00:32.386 --> 00:00:33.476
<v Sterling Baird>is there.

00:00:33.556 --> 00:00:35.226
<v Sterling Baird>Whereas like some people will use e-bikes

00:00:35.306 --> 00:00:38.166
<v Sterling Baird>for mountain biking and
they'll still get really good

00:00:38.246 --> 00:00:39.846
<v Sterling Baird>workouts out of it.

00:00:39.926 --> 00:00:43.457
<v In the room>It's not like we can choose
to not buy the e-bike.

00:00:43.537 --> 00:00:47.007
<v In the room>Oh, sorry — I bought it
yeah I bought it for almost

00:00:47.087 --> 00:00:49.287
<v Sterling Baird>like I literally bought it for everybody

00:00:49.367 --> 00:00:52.340
<v In the room>I think you know even though
it's fictional I think

00:00:52.420 --> 00:00:56.340
<v In the room>prime examples like Tony
Stark who you know he knows

00:00:56.420 --> 00:00:58.160
<v Carl Robison>all the math he knows
everything that he needs to

00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:01.406
<v Carl Robison>do where Jarvis is a support
to Tony Stark and not

00:01:01.486 --> 00:01:03.350
<v In the room>doing Tony Stark's work

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:05.490
<v Sterling Baird>We about to get YouTube famous.

00:01:05.570 --> 00:01:07.550
<v In the room>So, pick up a thousand likes on this.

00:01:07.630 --> 00:01:09.540
<v In the room>We're changing our career.

00:01:09.620 --> 00:01:12.480
<v In the room>Or maybe I misheard Audrey
but I think I heard her

00:01:12.560 --> 00:01:14.840
<v In the room>say reel — so like you know
we can make like a reel

00:01:14.920 --> 00:01:18.460
<v Carl Robison>of us like being this is good this is bad

00:01:18.540 --> 00:01:20.483
<v Sterling Baird>We'll probably call it good there.

00:01:20.563 --> 00:01:22.320
<v Sterling Baird>Thanks, Audrey, Carl, everybody.
